+2.  **Compute Pixel-wise Score:** For each Gaussian $G_i$, iterate over all pixels $P$ in its coverage region $\Omega_i$ [S2, unofficial]. Compute the pixel-wise score $r(P)$:
     $$ r(P) = \frac{1}{\alpha(P)} \left| \frac{\partial L(P)}{\partial \alpha(P)} \right| $$
     where $\alpha(P)$ is the opacity contribution of $G_i$ at pixel $P$, and $\frac{\partial L(P)}{\partial \alpha(P)}$ is the gradient of the loss at pixel $P$ with respect to that opacity [S2, unofficial].
